#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/FishLipidQuality.md:18
msgid ""
"Represents the fish/flesh lipid quality index, originally used to assess the "
"lipid quality of fish or flesh. It evaluates the proportion of the two most "
"critical marine omega -3 long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids: "
"eicosapentaenoic acid (EPA, $C20:5\\[\\\\omega-3\\]$) and docosahexaenoic "
"acid (DHA, $C22:6\\[\\\\omega-3\\]$)."
msgstr ""

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/FishLipidQuality.md:20
msgid ""
"From a human health perspective, a higher FLQ value is more desirable. EPA "
"and DHA play essential roles in biological processes, including reducing the "
"risk of cardiovascular diseases, hypertension, and inflammation. Because "
"this index specifically highlights these two fatty acids, it is particularly "
"suitable for evaluating marine products or foods enriched with marine "
"lipids. Higher values indicate a better nutritional quality of the lipid "
"fraction."
msgstr ""

