#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/SaturationIndex.md:10
msgid "SI"
msgstr "SI"

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/SaturationIndex.md:11
msgid "IS"
msgstr "IS"

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/SaturationIndex.md:15
msgid "Index of saturation"
msgstr "Индекс насыщения"

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/SaturationIndex.md:19
msgid ""
"Represents the saturation index, which evaluates the relationship between "
"specific saturated fatty acids (myristic C14:0, palmitic C16:0, and stearic "
"C18:0) and the total amount of unsaturated fatty acids (both monounsaturated "
"and polyunsaturated)."
msgstr ""

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Nutritional/SaturationIndex.md:21
msgid ""
"From a nutritional point of view, the SI value should be as low as possible. "
"This index serves as a straightforward indicator of the overall saturation "
"level of the lipids in a food product. A lower SI value suggests better "
"nutritional properties and higher lipid quality, as it reflects a higher "
"proportion of beneficial unsaturated fatty acids relative to saturated ones. "
"Diets with a lower saturation index are generally recommended to maintain "
"cardiovascular health and reduce the risk of related diseases."
msgstr ""

