#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Intraposition/Polyunsaturated-6ToPolyunsaturated-3.md:12
msgid "Omega -6 to omega -3"
msgstr "Омега -6 жирные кислоты к омега -3 жирным кислотам"

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Intraposition/Polyunsaturated-6ToPolyunsaturated-3.md:15
msgid ""
"Indicates the balance between these two types of essential polyunsaturated "
"fatty acids in the body."
msgstr ""

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Intraposition/Polyunsaturated-6ToPolyunsaturated-3.md:17
msgid ""
"_Inflammatory Balance_: Omega -6 and omega -3 fatty acids are precursors to "
"molecules that regulate inflammation. While omega -6 fatty acids are "
"generally pro-inflammatory, omega -3 fatty acids have anti-inflammatory "
"effects. An imbalance with a high proportion of omega -6 to omega -3 can "
"lead to chronic low-grade inflammation, which is associated with various "
"chronic diseases."
msgstr ""

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Intraposition/Polyunsaturated-6ToPolyunsaturated-3.md:18
msgid ""
"_Risk of Chronic Diseases_: A high n-6/n-3 ratio is linked to an increased "
"risk of cardiovascular disease, obesity, and other inflammatory conditions. "
"Conversely, a lower, more balanced ratio is considered beneficial for "
"preventing these health issues."
msgstr ""

#: src/FattyAcids/Ratio/Intraposition/Polyunsaturated-6ToPolyunsaturated-3.md:19
msgid ""
"_Cellular Health_: Both omega -6 and omega -3 fatty acids are crucial "
"components of cell membranes and are necessary for regulating blood pressure "
"and other bodily functions. The balance between them is vital for optimal "
"cellular function."
msgstr ""

